[
    {
        "content": "<p><code>grind</code> takes a list of proof terms or declaration names that it then can use in the proof.</p>\n<p>Its specializations <code>lia</code> and <code>grobner</code> don't (so whatever is needed needs to first be put in the local context via <code>have</code>). It would however be convenient if they did. Is this just an oversight, or is there a more conceptual reason why they don't?</p>\n<p>BTW, the <a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/4.34.0-rc2/The--grind--tactic/#grind-tactic\">Language Reference entry for <code>grind</code></a> apparently does not explain the complete syntax of <code>grind</code> (e.g., is it possible to add options to <code>grind</code> that reduce it to <code>lia</code> or <code>grobner</code> only?). <a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/4.34.0-rc2/Tactic-Proofs/Tactic-Reference/#lia\">The entries for <code>lia</code></a> and <a href=\"https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/4.34.0-rc2/Tactic-Proofs/Tactic-Reference/#grobner\"><code>grobner</code></a> only mention that they are \"a thin wrapper around the <code>grind</code> tactic\", but they don't say <em>how</em> this \"thin wrapper\" is actually defined.</p>",
        "id": 621650561,
        "sender_full_name": "Michael Stoll",
        "timestamp": 1788513664
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We can reproduce <code>lia</code> and <code>grind</code> from user space:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mod_lt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">decide</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">config</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Grind</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CutsatConfig</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toConfig</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">lia</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">z</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">config</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">({}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Grind</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">GrobnerConfig</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toConfig</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Note that for the first one, you need to add <code>lia</code> to the arguments, to pull in the lemmas marked <code>@[lia]</code>.</p>\n<p>I'll add support for arguments for both <code>lia</code> and <code>grobner</code>.</p>",
        "id": 623321312,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1789096248
    },
